{"condition": "B1", "run_id": "B1-dev-smoke", "checkpoint": "nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-BF16", "question_id": "financebench_id_03882", "document_id": "AMCOR_2020_10K", "split": "dev", "training_seed": null, "sampling_seed": null, "derived": false, "evaluation_signature": "7fccf29f38dbab599039975798a3cc0eab282a0636e456ae3381d47f32c1f884", "F": 1.0, "A": 0.0, "G": 0.0, "Ret": 0.0, "correct": 0, "grounded_success": 0, "reward": 0.0, "unresolved": false, "grader_version": "workshop-v1", "fabricated_citation": false, "stop_reason": "accepted_finish", "output_tokens": 1699, "total_reward": 0.0, "turns": 5, "submission": {"answer_type": "text", "value": "", "unit": "", "scale": "", "decision": "", "answer_text": "Amcor's FY2020 year\u2011end net accounts receivable was $1,615.9 million, as shown on the Consolidated Balance Sheet (in millions) as of June\u202f30\u202f2020.", "citations": [{"receipt_id": "r1", "document_id": "AMCOR_2020_10K", "page": 50}], "calc_id": ""}, "latency_s": 10.654709242051467, "tool_calls": 3, "calculator_used": false, "gold_page_read": true, "citation_count": 1, "visible_citations": 1, "raw_tool_chars": [2869, 2327, 366], "visible_tool_chars": [2920, 2378, 416], "truncated_observations": 0, "cost_usd": null, "trace_path": "results/paper_2026_rl4llm/B1-dev-smoke/rollouts/financebench_id_03882.json"}
{"condition": "B1", "run_id": "B1-dev-smoke", "checkpoint": "nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-BF16", "question_id": "financebench_id_01936", "document_id": "AMCOR_2023Q2_10Q", "split": "dev", "training_seed": null, "sampling_seed": null, "derived": false, "evaluation_signature": "7fccf29f38dbab599039975798a3cc0eab282a0636e456ae3381d47f32c1f884", "F": 1.0, "A": 0.0, "G": 1.0, "Ret": 1.0, "correct": 0, "grounded_success": 0, "reward": 0.0, "unresolved": true, "grader_version": "workshop-v1", "fabricated_citation": false, "judge_error": "RuntimeError", "stop_reason": "accepted_finish", "output_tokens": 959, "total_reward": 0.0, "turns": 3, "submission": {"answer_type": "text", "value": "", "unit": "", "scale": "", "decision": "", "answer_text": "As of the close of Q2 FY2023 (quarter ended December\u202f31\u202f2022), Amcor's restructuring liability totaled $93\u202fmillion, composed of $81\u202fmillion employee costs, $2\u202fmillion fixed\u2011asset\u2011related costs and $10\u202fmillion other costs (see Note\u202f6 \u2013 Restructuring, page\u202f15 of the 10\u2011Q, receipt\u202fr1). The liability stems from two principal initiatives: (1) restructuring activities related to the Russia\u2011Ukraine conflict, and (2) the Company's 2019 integration plan for the acquired Bemis operations, which was substantially completed by the end of fiscal year\u202f2022. During the three months ended December\u202f31\u202f2022, the Company recorded net restructuring charges of $2\u202fmillion; cash payments of $16\u202fmillion, and a reversal of unused amounts of $2\u202fmillion, reducing the liability from $118\u202fmillion at June\u202f30\u202f2022 to $93\u202fmillion at December\u202f31\u202f2022. The accruals are classified as other current and non\u2011current liabilities on the consolidated balance sheets.", "citations": [{"receipt_id": "r1", "document_id": "AMCOR_2023Q2_10Q", "page": 15}], "calc_id": ""}, "latency_s": 5.57190747896675, "tool_calls": 3, "calculator_used": false, "gold_page_read": true, "citation_count": 1, "visible_citations": 1, "raw_tool_chars": [2481, 1862, 1161], "visible_tool_chars": [2532, 1913, 1212], "truncated_observations": 0, "cost_usd": null, "trace_path": "results/paper_2026_rl4llm/B1-dev-smoke/rollouts/financebench_id_01936.json"}
